---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import EvidenceChart from '../components/EvidenceChart.astro';
import {
  memoryEvidence,
  irEvidence,
  providers,
  percent,
  full,
  mib,
} from '../lib/evidence';
import {
  report,
  workloads,
  range,
  largestRss,
  recovered,
} from '../lib/benchmarks';
---

<Base
  title="Benchmarks"
  description="Full LongMemEval-S and LoCoMo evidence retrieval, secondary BEIR results, native footprint and raw verification receipts. See wins, gaps and test limits together."
>
  <main id="main" class="shell evidence-page" data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="editorial-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">Evidence / 04 October 2026 / Engine fafa202</p>
      <h1>
        Small engine.
        <br />
        Open evidence.
      </h1>
      <p>
        Full retrieval runs. Clear baselines. Raw rankings you can check. These
        results measure source evidence retrieval; they do not measure final
        answer accuracy.
      </p>
    </header>
    <nav class="page-jump" aria-label="Benchmark sections">
      <a href="#overview">All results</a>
      <a href="#memory">Memory suites</a>
      <a href="#ir">Document retrieval</a>
      <a href="#footprint">Footprint</a>
      <a href="#method">Method & limits</a>
    </nav>
    <section id="overview" class="editorial-section">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">At a glance / Recall@10</p>
        <h2>Every result, in one table.</h2>
        <p>
          Higher is better. Different datasets use different source labels. Do
          not average these scores into one quality claim.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div
        class="table-scroll"
        role="region"
        aria-label="All retrieval results"
        tabindex="0"
      >
        <table class="evidence-table">
          <caption>Observed Recall@10, with full dataset scope</caption>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th scope="col">Suite / evidence</th>
              <th scope="col">Scored questions</th>
              {providers.map((p) => (
                <th scope="col">{p}</th>
              ))}
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {[...memoryEvidence, ...irEvidence].map((row) => (
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">
                  <a href={row.raw}>{row.name}</a>
                  <small>
                    {row.scope}
                    {row.docs
                      ? ` · ${row.docs.toLocaleString('en-US')} documents`
                      : ''}
                  </small>
                </th>
                <td>
                  {row.count.toLocaleString('en-US')}
                  <small>
                    {row.queried !== row.count
                      ? `${row.queried.toLocaleString('en-US')} queried`
                      : 'Full question set'}
                  </small>
                </td>
                {row.recall.map((value, i) => (
                  <td class={i === 0 ? 'native-score' : ''}>
                    {value === null ? '—' : percent(value) + '%'}
                  </td>
                ))}
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="chart-note">
        — means no complete published run. BEIR controls were recorded
        separately on 3 October. ArguAna hit work limits on 688 queries.{' '}
        <a href="#method">Read the limits ↓</a>
      </p>
      <aside class="evidence-status">
        <strong>Answer-quality scoring is pending.</strong>
        <p>
          The first GPT-6 Luna QA runs hit API rate limits. They cannot support
          a quality comparison. A rate-limited full LongMemEval-S QA rerun is in
          progress. No partial accuracy is published.
        </p>
      </aside>
    </section>
    <section id="memory" class="editorial-section">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">01 / Full memory datasets</p>
        <h2>
          Strong session recall.
          <br />A turn-level gap to close.
        </h2>
        <p>
          SQLite has slightly higher observed LongMemEval-S recall. Local
          Supermemory has slightly higher LoCoMo recall. instantKV leads LoCoMo
          nDCG@10 in this run. These small differences do not establish a
          statistically significant win.
        </p>
      </div>
      <EvidenceChart
        rows={memoryEvidence}
        id="memory-evidence"
        title="Recall and ranking quality"
      />
      <div class="feature-columns">
        <div>
          <h3>500 / 500 questions</h3>
          <p>
            LongMemEval-S uses session-level source labels. A correct source
            session can contain many turns; this is not exact-turn or QA
            accuracy.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>10 / 10 histories</h3>
          <p>
            LoCoMo queries all 1,986 questions. Recall uses 1,533 positive-label
            questions. 446 adversarial questions and seven unresolved references
            lack scored positive labels.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>0 failures, 0 truncations</h3>
          <p>
            All five complete retrieval files. Rankings were independently
            checked with pytrec_eval against official source labels.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="raw-links">
        <a href="/benchmark-data/full-retrieval/summary.json">Summary JSON ↗</a>
        <a href="/benchmark-data/full-retrieval/verification.json">
          Verification receipts ↗
        </a>
        <a href="/docs/full-retrieval/">Full run notes ↗</a>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section id="ir" class="editorial-section">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">02 / Secondary BEIR tests</p>
        <h2>
          Useful lexical retrieval.
          <br />
          Room beyond keywords.
        </h2>
        <p>
          Full SciFact, ArguAna and NFCorpus question sets. instantKV uses
          bounded BM25 with English stemming. The local Supermemory control uses
          bge-base embeddings without a reranker.
        </p>
      </div>
      <EvidenceChart
        rows={irEvidence}
        id="ir-evidence"
        title="Full document retrieval sets"
      />
      <p class="evidence-caveat">
        Current native runs against recorded same-host controls. ArguAna: zero
        rejected queries; 688 truncated and 1,149 reduced. NFCorpus remains a
        loss. These results do not represent hosted Supermemory.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section id="footprint" class="editorial-section">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">03 / Native process measurements</p>
        <h2>Keep the memory layer small.</h2>
        <p>
          Measured on an Apple M4 Pro, 24 GiB RAM, macOS 27.0 ARM64. No
          embedding model in the instantKV process. Sampled RSS does not
          establish peak memory.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="measurement-grid">
        <div>
          <span>Native binary</span>
          <strong>{mib(report.binary_bytes)} MiB</strong>
          <p>Measured source build.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <span>LongMemEval-S server RSS</span>
          <strong>
            {mib(
              full.suites['longmemeval-s'].instantkv.largest_sampled_rss_bytes,
            )}{' '}
            MiB
          </strong>
          <p>Largest sampled Rust process RSS.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <span>LoCoMo server RSS</span>
          <strong>
            {mib(full.suites.locomo.instantkv.largest_sampled_rss_bytes)} MiB
          </strong>
          <p>Largest sampled Rust process RSS.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <h3 class="subsection-title">Separate structured-memory workload</h3>
      <p>
        Three fresh databases. 10,000 records each, 512-byte content plus
        metadata. Warm loopback HTTP, one request at a time. Immediate durable
        commits.
      </p>
      <div
        class="latency-chart"
        aria-label="Median run p95 latency in milliseconds, linear zero to eight millisecond scale"
      >
        <div class="chart-heading">
          <h3>p95 by operation</h3>
          <span class="eyebrow">Lower is better / ms</span>
        </div>
        {workloads
          .filter((w) =>
            ['save', 'topic', 'tag', 'time', 'exact', 'forget'].includes(w.id),
          )
          .map((w) => (
            <div class="latency-row">
              <span>{w.name}</span>
              <div class="latency-track">
                <span style={`width:${(w.p95 / 8) * 100}%`}></span>
              </div>
              <strong>{w.p95.toFixed(3)}</strong>
            </div>
          ))}
        <div class="latency-axis" aria-hidden="true">
          <span>0 ms</span>
          <span>4 ms</span>
          <span>8 ms</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div
        class="table-scroll"
        role="region"
        aria-label="All structured memory latency measurements"
        tabindex="0"
      >
        <table class="evidence-table">
          <caption>Milliseconds; median of three run percentiles</caption>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th scope="col">Operation</th>
              <th scope="col">p50</th>
              <th scope="col">p95</th>
              <th scope="col">p99</th>
              <th scope="col">p95 range</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {workloads.map((w) => (
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">
                  {w.name}
                  <small>{w.detail}</small>
                </th>
                <td>{w.p50.toFixed(3)}</td>
                <td>{w.p95.toFixed(3)}</td>
                <td>{w.p99.toFixed(3)}</td>
                <td>{w.p95Range}</td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="chart-note">
        Idle RSS{' '}
        {range(
          report.runs.map((r) => r.idle_rss_bytes / 1024 ** 2),
          2,
        )}{' '}
        MiB. Largest sampled RSS {mib(largestRss)} MiB in this separate
        workload. {recovered.toLocaleString('en-US')} / 30,000 records recovered
        after abrupt process restarts. No device power-loss test.{' '}
        <a href="/benchmark-data/memory/mac-arm64.json">
          Raw structured-memory runs ↗
        </a>
      </p>
    </section>
    <section id="method" class="editorial-section">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">04 / How to read the evidence</p>
        <h2>Measure the actual boundary.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="method-grid">
        <div>
          <h3>Same source data</h3>
          <p>
            Providers receive the same source documents, lossless chunks and
            questions. SQLite uses the same 64 KiB page and 64-page response
            bound as instantKV. The engine is frozen at{' '}
            {full.runtime_commit.slice(0, 7)}.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Different process scopes</h3>
          <p>
            SQLite is in-process and includes the Python runner in RSS. Local
            Supermemory retains corpus scopes in one server per suite. Rust RSS
            is the native server. These figures do not support a RAM efficiency
            ratio.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Shared hardware load</h3>
          <p>
            Memory suites ran in parallel. Their timings cannot establish
            isolated speed ratios. The structured-memory latency chart is a
            separate sequential workload; it excludes inference.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Local control, limited pipeline</h3>
          <p>
            Supermemory local v0.0.8 uses direct embedding retrieval. Model
            extraction, query rewriting and reranking are disabled. Its full
            hosted system is not measured.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Frozen evaluations</h3>
          <p>
            These test questions have been exposed. No engine tuning occurred
            during the full runs. Use separate development data for further
            changes. Untouched checkpoint evaluations remain part of the plan.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Still to measure</h3>
          <p>
            Official end-to-end QA, LongMemEval-V2, AMA-Bench, BEAM, Mem0, Zep,
            dense-vector controls and 100K–10M+ record tests remain incomplete.
            Phone latency, battery and native bindings remain planned.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="raw-links">
        <a href="/docs/benchmarks/">Reproduction guide →</a>
        <a href="/docs/evaluation-policy/">Evaluation policy →</a>
        <a href="/docs/performance/">Performance details →</a>
        <a href="/blog/lightweight-memory-benchmarks/">Engineering notes →</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Base>
